# Trivy allow-list for the production image release scan (infra/.github/workflows/deploy.yml).
#
# These are freshly-disclosed CVEs in BUILD/DEV tooling that ships inside the
# runtime images but is never on any request path. They cannot be removed or
# patched yet:
#
#  - The migrate job needs drizzle-kit (runs the SQL migrations) and tsx (runs
#    the seed), and both bundle the `esbuild` binary — a Go program that embeds
#    the Go standard library. The advisories below are in that embedded stdlib
#    and in golang.org/x/text.
#  - The native TypeScript 7 compiler (@typescript/typescript-linux-x64) embeds
#    the same Go stdlib.
#
# The scan already runs with ignore-unfixed=true, so every entry here is FIXED
# upstream — the tools simply have not shipped a release rebuilt on the patched
# Go toolchain yet. Remove each ID once esbuild / drizzle-kit / tsx / typescript
# publish a rebuilt binary. Reviewed: 2026-07-29.

# Go stdlib: os.Root symlink-following directory traversal
CVE-2026-39822
# Go stdlib: net/mail DoS via crafted email inputs
CVE-2026-39820
# Go stdlib: net/mail DoS via pathological address parsing
CVE-2026-42499
# Go stdlib: mime DoS via crafted header
CVE-2026-42504
# Go stdlib security update (ELSA-2026-22121)
CVE-2026-39836
# golang.org/x/text: norm.Iter infinite loop on crafted input
CVE-2026-56852
